-- Regression fixture: a project-local override must reach EMBEDDED importers
-- too, not just the top-level module.
--
--     main  ->  actus-schedule (embedded)  ->  daydate
--                                              ^
--                        ./daydate.l4 (this directory) must win here as well
--
-- `actus-schedule` is served by the embedded stdlib; it imports `daydate`, and
-- so does the project (see the sibling daydate.l4). Option B′ ranks the project
-- root above the embedded stdlib, and the shadow warning promises in so many
-- words that "the [chosen] copy is used wherever this module is imported" — so
-- the embedded importer must bind to the project copy, giving one source per
-- module name across the whole build.
--
-- It did not. An embedded importer's own URI used to be the bare
-- `file://actus-schedule.l4`, so `takeDirectory` of it was ".", and its
-- candidate URI for `daydate` collided with the URI the embedded `daydate` was
-- registered under. The VFS tier hit that before library resolution ever ran,
-- and this file checked CLEAN — with `actus-schedule` type-checked against the
-- embedded `daydate` while `main` and every other module saw the project copy.
--
-- The positive control for this fixture is ../../embedded-diamond/main.l4:
-- the same embedded closure, with no project-local override, checks clean.
IMPORT `actus-schedule`
